# Drop-in for the compresso-recsys repository root (0.4.0 release).
# Before tagging, fill in: ORCIDs, release date, Zenodo DOI (concept DOI), and
# the ECIR 2027 paper details once accepted. Validate with:
#   pip install cffconvert && cffconvert --validate
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use compresso-recsys in your research, please cite the paper in
  "preferred-citation". To cite this exact software release, use the
  metadata below (version and DOI).
title: "compresso-recsys"
abstract: >-
  A modular Python toolkit for recommender-system research: dataset loaders and
  a portable ZIP checkpoint format for reproducible splits, streaming ranking
  evaluation, paired statistical comparison of recommenders, and collaborative,
  sequential, cold-start and multimodal models behind one evaluation and
  serving interface.
type: software
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-11-XX"            # TODO: set at tag time
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"          # TODO: Zenodo concept DOI (all versions)
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/zombak79/compresso-recsys"
url: "https://zombak79.github.io/compresso-recsys/"
keywords:
  - recommender systems
  - evaluation
  - statistical significance testing
  - reproducibility
  - datasets
  - cold-start
  - sequential recommendation
